IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cdba-nouns`
IMPORT `cdba-calendar`
IMPORT `cdba-reg-definitions`
IMPORT `cdba-reg-eligibility`

-- Tests for Regulations ss 2, 2.1 and 3. Every expected value is decided from the text
-- of the section, under the readings recorded in NOTES.md (fork F1: a criterion is met
-- for a month when it holds throughout the month).
--
-- Each builder below makes an otherwise eligible person (born 10 May 1990, DTC-eligible,
-- resident, a Canadian citizen, return filed, no spouse, no custody, no suspension) and
-- varies only what the test is about.

§ `Regulations s 2 -- tests`

`the baseline birth date` MEANS YMD 1990 5 10
`August 2025` MEANS YMD 2025 8 15

-- Varies the birth date and the month asked about.
GIVEN dob   IS A DATE
      month IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Person facts for a month`
`an otherwise eligible person born on` dob `asking about` month MEANS
    `Person facts for a month` WITH
        `the month asked about`                       IS month
        `date of birth`                               IS dob
        `a DTC-eligible individual throughout the month` IS TRUE
        `resident in Canada for the purposes of the Income Tax Act throughout the month` IS TRUE
        `a Canadian citizen`                          IS TRUE
        `a permanent resident`                        IS FALSE
        `a temporary resident`                        IS FALSE
        `months resident in Canada immediately before the month` IS 0
        `a protected person`                          IS FALSE
        `an Indian as defined in subsection 2(1) of the Indian Act` IS FALSE
        `the custody under a sentence`                IS NOTHING
        `a return of income was filed for the last taxation year that ended before the payment period began` IS TRUE
        `a cohabiting spouse or common-law partner on the last day of the month before` IS FALSE
        `the cohabiting spouse or common-law partner filed a return of income for that year` IS FALSE
        `the Minister waived the spouse or partner condition` IS FALSE
        `the suspension the beneficiary asked for`    IS NOTHING

-- Varies the DTC fact, residence, the five kinds of person and the return.
GIVEN dtc      IS A BOOLEAN
      resident IS A BOOLEAN
      citizen  IS A BOOLEAN
      pr       IS A BOOLEAN
      temp     IS A BOOLEAN
      months   IS A NUMBER
      prot     IS A BOOLEAN
      indian   IS A BOOLEAN
      filed    IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Person facts for a month`
`an otherwise eligible person in August 2025 with status` dtc resident citizen pr temp months prot indian filed MEANS
    `Person facts for a month` WITH
        `the month asked about`                       IS `August 2025`
        `date of birth`                               IS `the baseline birth date`
        `a DTC-eligible individual throughout the month` IS dtc
        `resident in Canada for the purposes of the Income Tax Act throughout the month` IS resident
        `a Canadian citizen`                          IS citizen
        `a permanent resident`                        IS pr
        `a temporary resident`                        IS temp
        `months resident in Canada immediately before the month` IS months
        `a protected person`                          IS prot
        `an Indian as defined in subsection 2(1) of the Indian Act` IS indian
        `the custody under a sentence`                IS NOTHING
        `a return of income was filed for the last taxation year that ended before the payment period began` IS filed
        `a cohabiting spouse or common-law partner on the last day of the month before` IS FALSE
        `the cohabiting spouse or common-law partner filed a return of income for that year` IS FALSE
        `the Minister waived the spouse or partner condition` IS FALSE
        `the suspension the beneficiary asked for`    IS NOTHING

-- Varies the month and the custody.
GIVEN month   IS A DATE
      custody IS A MAYBE `Custody under a sentence`
GIVETH A `Person facts for a month`
`an otherwise eligible person in the month` month `with custody` custody MEANS
    `Person facts for a month` WITH
        `the month asked about`                       IS month
        `date of birth`                               IS `the baseline birth date`
        `a DTC-eligible individual throughout the month` IS TRUE
        `resident in Canada for the purposes of the Income Tax Act throughout the month` IS TRUE
        `a Canadian citizen`                          IS TRUE
        `a permanent resident`                        IS FALSE
        `a temporary resident`                        IS FALSE
        `months resident in Canada immediately before the month` IS 0
        `a protected person`                          IS FALSE
        `an Indian as defined in subsection 2(1) of the Indian Act` IS FALSE
        `the custody under a sentence`                IS custody
        `a return of income was filed for the last taxation year that ended before the payment period began` IS TRUE
        `a cohabiting spouse or common-law partner on the last day of the month before` IS FALSE
        `the cohabiting spouse or common-law partner filed a return of income for that year` IS FALSE
        `the Minister waived the spouse or partner condition` IS FALSE
        `the suspension the beneficiary asked for`    IS NOTHING

-- Varies the spouse or partner facts.
GIVEN spouse  IS A BOOLEAN
      filed   IS A BOOLEAN
      waived  IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Person facts for a month`
`an otherwise eligible person in August 2025 with spouse` spouse filed waived MEANS
    `Person facts for a month` WITH
        `the month asked about`                       IS `August 2025`
        `date of birth`                               IS `the baseline birth date`
        `a DTC-eligible individual throughout the month` IS TRUE
        `resident in Canada for the purposes of the Income Tax Act throughout the month` IS TRUE
        `a Canadian citizen`                          IS TRUE
        `a permanent resident`                        IS FALSE
        `a temporary resident`                        IS FALSE
        `months resident in Canada immediately before the month` IS 0
        `a protected person`                          IS FALSE
        `an Indian as defined in subsection 2(1) of the Indian Act` IS FALSE
        `the custody under a sentence`                IS NOTHING
        `a return of income was filed for the last taxation year that ended before the payment period began` IS TRUE
        `a cohabiting spouse or common-law partner on the last day of the month before` IS spouse
        `the cohabiting spouse or common-law partner filed a return of income for that year` IS filed
        `the Minister waived the spouse or partner condition` IS waived
        `the suspension the beneficiary asked for`    IS NOTHING

-- Varies the month and the suspension.
GIVEN month IS A DATE
      susp  IS A MAYBE `Suspension at the beneficiary's request`
GIVETH A `Person facts for a month`
`an otherwise eligible person in the month` month `with suspension` susp MEANS
    `Person facts for a month` WITH
        `the month asked about`                       IS month
        `date of birth`                               IS `the baseline birth date`
        `a DTC-eligible individual throughout the month` IS TRUE
        `resident in Canada for the purposes of the Income Tax Act throughout the month` IS TRUE
        `a Canadian citizen`                          IS TRUE
        `a permanent resident`                        IS FALSE
        `a temporary resident`                        IS FALSE
        `months resident in Canada immediately before the month` IS 0
        `a protected person`                          IS FALSE
        `an Indian as defined in subsection 2(1) of the Indian Act` IS FALSE
        `the custody under a sentence`                IS NOTHING
        `a return of income was filed for the last taxation year that ended before the payment period began` IS TRUE
        `a cohabiting spouse or common-law partner on the last day of the month before` IS FALSE
        `the cohabiting spouse or common-law partner filed a return of income for that year` IS FALSE
        `the Minister waived the spouse or partner condition` IS FALSE
        `the suspension the beneficiary asked for`    IS susp

§§ `s 2(1) -- the baseline person, and the month floor`

#ASSERT `the person is eligible to receive an allocation for the month` (`an otherwise eligible person born on` `the baseline birth date` `asking about` `August 2025`)

-- "any month after May 2025": June 2025 is the first month, May 2025 is not.
#ASSERT `the person is eligible to receive an allocation for the month` (`an otherwise eligible person born on` `the baseline birth date` `asking about` (YMD 2025 6 15))
#ASSERT NOT `the person is eligible to receive an allocation for the month` (`an otherwise eligible person born on` `the baseline birth date` `asking about` (YMD 2025 5 31))
#ASSERT NOT `the person is eligible to receive an allocation for the month` (`an otherwise eligible person born on` `the baseline birth date` `asking about` (YMD 2024 12 1))
#ASSERT `the month is after May 2025` (YMD 2025 6 1)
#ASSERT NOT `the month is after May 2025` (YMD 2025 5 31)

§§ `s 2(1)(a) and (2) -- age, throughout the month`

-- At least 18 throughout August 2025 means the 18th birthday is on or before 1 August.
#ASSERT `at least 18 years of age but not more than 65 years of age throughout the month` (YMD 2007 8 1) (YMD 2025 8 20)
#ASSERT NOT `at least 18 years of age but not more than 65 years of age throughout the month` (YMD 2007 8 2) (YMD 2025 8 20)
#ASSERT NOT `at least 18 years of age but not more than 65 years of age throughout the month` (YMD 2007 8 31) (YMD 2025 8 20)
#ASSERT `at least 18 years of age but not more than 65 years of age throughout the month` (YMD 2007 8 2) (YMD 2025 9 20)
#ASSERT `at least 18 years of age but not more than 65 years of age throughout the month` (YMD 2007 8 31) (YMD 2025 9 20)
-- Whole-person tests on the same edge: born on the 1st, 2nd and last day.
#ASSERT `the person is eligible to receive an allocation for the month` (`an otherwise eligible person born on` (YMD 2007 8 1) `asking about` (YMD 2025 8 15))
#ASSERT NOT `the person is eligible to receive an allocation for the month` (`an otherwise eligible person born on` (YMD 2007 8 2) `asking about` (YMD 2025 8 15))
#ASSERT NOT `the person is eligible to receive an allocation for the month` (`an otherwise eligible person born on` (YMD 2007 8 31) `asking about` (YMD 2025 8 15))
#ASSERT `the person is eligible to receive an allocation for the month` (`an otherwise eligible person born on` (YMD 2007 8 31) `asking about` (YMD 2025 9 15))

-- Not more than 65: the 65th birthday must be on or after the last day of the month.
-- Born 31 July 1960: 65th birthday 31 July 2025, the last day of July.
#ASSERT `at least 18 years of age but not more than 65 years of age throughout the month` (YMD 1960 7 31) (YMD 2025 7 10)
#ASSERT NOT `at least 18 years of age but not more than 65 years of age throughout the month` (YMD 1960 8 1) (YMD 2025 8 10)
#ASSERT NOT `at least 18 years of age but not more than 65 years of age throughout the month` (YMD 1960 8 15) (YMD 2025 8 10)
#ASSERT `at least 18 years of age but not more than 65 years of age throughout the month` (YMD 1960 8 31) (YMD 2025 8 10)
-- (2): in the month of the 65th birthday the person is still eligible, even when the
-- birthday is not on the last day. The month after, they are not.
#ASSERT `the person turns 65 years of age in the month` (YMD 1960 8 1) (YMD 2025 8 20)
#ASSERT `the person turns 65 years of age in the month` (YMD 1960 8 15) (YMD 2025 8 20)
#ASSERT `the person turns 65 years of age in the month` (YMD 1960 8 31) (YMD 2025 8 20)
#ASSERT NOT `the person turns 65 years of age in the month` (YMD 1960 8 15) (YMD 2025 9 20)
#ASSERT NOT `the person turns 65 years of age in the month` (YMD 1960 8 15) (YMD 2025 7 20)
#ASSERT `the person is eligible to receive an allocation for the month` (`an otherwise eligible person born on` (YMD 1960 8 1) `asking about` (YMD 2025 7 15))
#ASSERT `the person is eligible to receive an allocation for the month` (`an otherwise eligible person born on` (YMD 1960 8 1) `asking about` (YMD 2025 8 15))
#ASSERT NOT `the person is eligible to receive an allocation for the month` (`an otherwise eligible person born on` (YMD 1960 8 1) `asking about` (YMD 2025 9 15))
#ASSERT `the person is eligible to receive an allocation for the month` (`an otherwise eligible person born on` (YMD 1960 8 15) `asking about` (YMD 2025 8 15))
#ASSERT NOT `the person is eligible to receive an allocation for the month` (`an otherwise eligible person born on` (YMD 1960 8 15) `asking about` (YMD 2025 9 15))
#ASSERT `the person is eligible to receive an allocation for the month` (`an otherwise eligible person born on` (YMD 1960 7 31) `asking about` (YMD 2025 7 15))
#ASSERT `the person is eligible to receive an allocation for the month` (`an otherwise eligible person born on` (YMD 1960 7 31) `asking about` (YMD 2025 7 31))
#ASSERT NOT `the person is eligible to receive an allocation for the month` (`an otherwise eligible person born on` (YMD 1960 7 31) `asking about` (YMD 2025 8 15))
-- Fork F2: a person born on 29 February attains 65 on 28 February in 2065 (a year with
-- no 29 February), so February 2065 is their last eligible month and March 2065 is not.
#ASSERT `the person is eligible to receive an allocation for the month` (`an otherwise eligible person born on` (YMD 2000 2 29) `asking about` (YMD 2065 2 10))
#ASSERT NOT `the person is eligible to receive an allocation for the month` (`an otherwise eligible person born on` (YMD 2000 2 29) `asking about` (YMD 2065 3 10))

§§ `s 2(1)(b) -- DTC-eligible individual, a borrowed term asked as a fact`

#ASSERT NOT `the person is eligible to receive an allocation for the month` (`an otherwise eligible person in August 2025 with status` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT `a DTC-eligible individual for the month` (`an otherwise eligible person in August 2025 with status` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `a DTC-eligible individual for the month` (`an otherwise eligible person in August 2025 with status` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE TRUE)

§§ `s 2(1)(c) -- resident in Canada, and one of five kinds of person`

-- Each of the five kinds, alone, is enough.
#ASSERT `the person is eligible to receive an allocation for the month` (`an otherwise eligible person in August 2025 with status` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT `the person is eligible to receive an allocation for the month` (`an otherwise eligible person in August 2025 with status` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT `the person is eligible to receive an allocation for the month` (`an otherwise eligible person in August 2025 with status` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 TRUE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT `the person is eligible to receive an allocation for the month` (`an otherwise eligible person in August 2025 with status` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE TRUE TRUE)
-- A temporary resident needs the 18 months immediately before the month: 17 is not
-- enough, 18 is, and 30 is.
#ASSERT NOT `the person is eligible to receive an allocation for the month` (`an otherwise eligible person in August 2025 with status` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE 17 FALSE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT `the person is eligible to receive an allocation for the month` (`an otherwise eligible person in August 2025 with status` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE 18 FALSE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT `the person is eligible to receive an allocation for the month` (`an otherwise eligible person in August 2025 with status` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE 30 FALSE FALSE TRUE)
-- None of the five: not eligible, however long they have lived here.
#ASSERT NOT `the person is eligible to receive an allocation for the month` (`an otherwise eligible person in August 2025 with status` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE 120 FALSE FALSE TRUE)
-- A citizen who is not resident in Canada for the purposes of the Income Tax Act.
#ASSERT NOT `the person is eligible to receive an allocation for the month` (`an otherwise eligible person in August 2025 with status` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `resident in Canada and one of the listed kinds of person` (`an otherwise eligible person in August 2025 with status` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE TRUE)

§§ `s 2(1)(d) and (3) -- custody under a sentence of two years or more`

`a qualifying custody from 20 June 2025` MEANS `Custody under a sentence` WITH
    `the sentence of imprisonment is of two years or more` IS TRUE
    `the sentence is to be served in a penitentiary by virtue of an Act of Parliament` IS TRUE
    `the first day in custody` IS YMD 2025 6 20
    `the release that ended the custody` IS NOTHING

`the same custody ended by expiry on 10 September 2025` MEANS `Custody under a sentence` WITH
    `the sentence of imprisonment is of two years or more` IS TRUE
    `the sentence is to be served in a penitentiary by virtue of an Act of Parliament` IS TRUE
    `the first day in custody` IS YMD 2025 6 20
    `the release that ended the custody` IS JUST (`Release event` WITH
        `the day of the release` IS YMD 2025 9 10
        `the way of the release` IS `release at the expiry of the sentence`
        `the parole or statutory release was terminated or revoked` IS FALSE)

`the same custody ended by expiry on 1 September 2025` MEANS `Custody under a sentence` WITH
    `the sentence of imprisonment is of two years or more` IS TRUE
    `the sentence is to be served in a penitentiary by virtue of an Act of Parliament` IS TRUE
    `the first day in custody` IS YMD 2025 6 20
    `the release that ended the custody` IS JUST (`Release event` WITH
        `the day of the release` IS YMD 2025 9 1
        `the way of the release` IS `release at the expiry of the sentence`
        `the parole or statutory release was terminated or revoked` IS FALSE)

`the same custody ended by expiry on 31 August 2025` MEANS `Custody under a sentence` WITH
    `the sentence of imprisonment is of two years or more` IS TRUE
    `the sentence is to be served in a penitentiary by virtue of an Act of Parliament` IS TRUE
    `the first day in custody` IS YMD 2025 6 20
    `the release that ended the custody` IS JUST (`Release event` WITH
        `the day of the release` IS YMD 2025 8 31
        `the way of the release` IS `release at the expiry of the sentence`
        `the parole or statutory release was terminated or revoked` IS FALSE)

`the same custody with a parole on 10 September 2025 that was revoked` MEANS `Custody under a sentence` WITH
    `the sentence of imprisonment is of two years or more` IS TRUE
    `the sentence is to be served in a penitentiary by virtue of an Act of Parliament` IS TRUE
    `the first day in custody` IS YMD 2025 6 20
    `the release that ended the custody` IS JUST (`Release event` WITH
        `the day of the release` IS YMD 2025 9 10
        `the way of the release` IS `release on parole`
        `the parole or statutory release was terminated or revoked` IS TRUE)

`a custody under a sentence of less than two years` MEANS `Custody under a sentence` WITH
    `the sentence of imprisonment is of two years or more` IS FALSE
    `the sentence is to be served in a penitentiary by virtue of an Act of Parliament` IS TRUE
    `the first day in custody` IS YMD 2025 6 20
    `the release that ended the custody` IS NOTHING

`a custody under a sentence not served in a penitentiary` MEANS `Custody under a sentence` WITH
    `the sentence of imprisonment is of two years or more` IS TRUE
    `the sentence is to be served in a penitentiary by virtue of an Act of Parliament` IS FALSE
    `the first day in custody` IS YMD 2025 6 20
    `the release that ended the custody` IS NOTHING

-- Custody that began on 20 June 2025 and has not ended: June is the first month of the
-- incarceration (s 2(3)), July is a month in custody and is not saved by s 2(3).
#ASSERT `the person is eligible to receive an allocation for the month` (`an otherwise eligible person in the month` (YMD 2025 6 15) `with custody` (JUST `a qualifying custody from 20 June 2025`))
#ASSERT `the month is the first month of the incarceration or the month of the release` (`an otherwise eligible person in the month` (YMD 2025 6 15) `with custody` (JUST `a qualifying custody from 20 June 2025`))
#ASSERT NOT `the person is eligible to receive an allocation for the month` (`an otherwise eligible person in the month` (YMD 2025 7 15) `with custody` (JUST `a qualifying custody from 20 June 2025`))
#ASSERT NOT `the month is the first month of the incarceration or the month of the release` (`an otherwise eligible person in the month` (YMD 2025 7 15) `with custody` (JUST `a qualifying custody from 20 June 2025`))
#ASSERT NOT `not incarcerated under a qualifying sentence in the month` (`an otherwise eligible person in the month` (YMD 2025 7 15) `with custody` (JUST `a qualifying custody from 20 June 2025`))
-- The month before the custody began is untouched.
#ASSERT `the person is eligible to receive an allocation for the month` (`an otherwise eligible person in the month` (YMD 2025 6 15) `with custody` NOTHING)
-- Ended by expiry on 10 September: August is in custody (not eligible), September is
-- the month of the release (eligible), October is free.
#ASSERT NOT `the person is eligible to receive an allocation for the month` (`an otherwise eligible person in the month` (YMD 2025 8 15) `with custody` (JUST `the same custody ended by expiry on 10 September 2025`))
#ASSERT `the person is eligible to receive an allocation for the month` (`an otherwise eligible person in the month` (YMD 2025 9 15) `with custody` (JUST `the same custody ended by expiry on 10 September 2025`))
#ASSERT `the person is eligible to receive an allocation for the month` (`an otherwise eligible person in the month` (YMD 2025 10 15) `with custody` (JUST `the same custody ended by expiry on 10 September 2025`))
-- Released on the first day of September: still the month of the release.
#ASSERT NOT `the person is eligible to receive an allocation for the month` (`an otherwise eligible person in the month` (YMD 2025 8 15) `with custody` (JUST `the same custody ended by expiry on 1 September 2025`))
#ASSERT `the person is eligible to receive an allocation for the month` (`an otherwise eligible person in the month` (YMD 2025 9 15) `with custody` (JUST `the same custody ended by expiry on 1 September 2025`))
-- Released on the last day of August: August is the month of the release, September free.
#ASSERT `the person is eligible to receive an allocation for the month` (`an otherwise eligible person in the month` (YMD 2025 8 15) `with custody` (JUST `the same custody ended by expiry on 31 August 2025`))
#ASSERT `the person is eligible to receive an allocation for the month` (`an otherwise eligible person in the month` (YMD 2025 9 15) `with custody` (JUST `the same custody ended by expiry on 31 August 2025`))
-- A parole that was revoked is not a "release": the person is still in custody in
-- September and October, and September is not a month of release.
#ASSERT NOT `the person is eligible to receive an allocation for the month` (`an otherwise eligible person in the month` (YMD 2025 9 15) `with custody` (JUST `the same custody with a parole on 10 September 2025 that was revoked`))
#ASSERT NOT `the person is eligible to receive an allocation for the month` (`an otherwise eligible person in the month` (YMD 2025 10 15) `with custody` (JUST `the same custody with a parole on 10 September 2025 that was revoked`))
-- A sentence under two years, or one not served in a penitentiary, does not bite.
#ASSERT `the person is eligible to receive an allocation for the month` (`an otherwise eligible person in the month` (YMD 2025 7 15) `with custody` (JUST `a custody under a sentence of less than two years`))
#ASSERT `the person is eligible to receive an allocation for the month` (`an otherwise eligible person in the month` (YMD 2025 7 15) `with custody` (JUST `a custody under a sentence not served in a penitentiary`))

§§ `s 2(1)(e) -- the return of income`

#ASSERT NOT `the person is eligible to receive an allocation for the month` (`an otherwise eligible person in August 2025 with status` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `a return of income filed for the last taxation year that ended before the payment period` (`an otherwise eligible person in August 2025 with status` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE)

§§ `s 2(4) and (5) -- the cohabiting spouse or common-law partner`

-- No spouse or partner: the condition has nothing to bite on.
#ASSERT `the person is eligible to receive an allocation for the month` (`an otherwise eligible person in August 2025 with spouse` FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- A spouse who has filed: eligible. A spouse who has not: not eligible. Waived: eligible.
#ASSERT `the person is eligible to receive an allocation for the month` (`an otherwise eligible person in August 2025 with spouse` TRUE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the person is eligible to receive an allocation for the month` (`an otherwise eligible person in August 2025 with spouse` TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `the person is eligible to receive an allocation for the month` (`an otherwise eligible person in August 2025 with spouse` TRUE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `the cohabiting spouse or common-law partner condition is satisfied` (`an otherwise eligible person in August 2025 with spouse` TRUE FALSE TRUE)
-- Where the person stands.
#ASSERT `where the person stands on the cohabiting spouse or common-law partner condition` (`an otherwise eligible person in August 2025 with spouse` FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `the condition does not apply: no cohabiting spouse or common-law partner`
#ASSERT `where the person stands on the cohabiting spouse or common-law partner condition` (`an otherwise eligible person in August 2025 with spouse` TRUE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS `the condition is met`
#ASSERT `where the person stands on the cohabiting spouse or common-law partner condition` (`an otherwise eligible person in August 2025 with spouse` TRUE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS `the condition is not met, and the Minister has waived it`
#ASSERT `where the person stands on the cohabiting spouse or common-law partner condition` (`an otherwise eligible person in August 2025 with spouse` TRUE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `the condition is not met, and the Minister may waive it if satisfied that it is unreasonable or impracticable`
-- The waiver is the Minister's judgment: it follows their satisfaction and nothing else.
#ASSERT `the Minister may waive the condition in subsection 2(4)` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the Minister may waive the condition in subsection 2(4)` FALSE
-- The named circumstances inform the Minister; none of them is a waiver by itself.
#ASSERT `a circumstance named in subsection 2(5) is present` TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `a circumstance named in subsection 2(5) is present` FALSE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `a circumstance named in subsection 2(5) is present` FALSE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `a circumstance named in subsection 2(5) is present` FALSE FALSE FALSE

§§ `s 2(6) -- a suspension the beneficiary asked for (fork F12: payment suspended throughout the month)`

`a suspension from 15 September 2025 until payment resumed in December 2025` MEANS `Suspension at the beneficiary's request` WITH
    `the day the suspension took effect` IS YMD 2025 9 15
    `a day in the month payment resumed` IS JUST (YMD 2025 12 4)

`a suspension from 1 October 2025 until payment resumed in December 2025` MEANS `Suspension at the beneficiary's request` WITH
    `the day the suspension took effect` IS YMD 2025 10 1
    `a day in the month payment resumed` IS JUST (YMD 2025 12 4)

`a suspension from 31 August 2025 with no resumption` MEANS `Suspension at the beneficiary's request` WITH
    `the day the suspension took effect` IS YMD 2025 8 31
    `a day in the month payment resumed` IS NOTHING

-- Taking effect on the 15th: September is not suspended throughout, so it stays payable;
-- October and November are, and December (the month payment resumed) is payable again.
#ASSERT `the person is eligible to receive an allocation for the month` (`an otherwise eligible person in the month` (YMD 2025 8 15) `with suspension` (JUST `a suspension from 15 September 2025 until payment resumed in December 2025`))
#ASSERT `the person is eligible to receive an allocation for the month` (`an otherwise eligible person in the month` (YMD 2025 9 15) `with suspension` (JUST `a suspension from 15 September 2025 until payment resumed in December 2025`))
#ASSERT NOT `the person is eligible to receive an allocation for the month` (`an otherwise eligible person in the month` (YMD 2025 10 15) `with suspension` (JUST `a suspension from 15 September 2025 until payment resumed in December 2025`))
#ASSERT NOT `the person is eligible to receive an allocation for the month` (`an otherwise eligible person in the month` (YMD 2025 11 15) `with suspension` (JUST `a suspension from 15 September 2025 until payment resumed in December 2025`))
#ASSERT `the person is eligible to receive an allocation for the month` (`an otherwise eligible person in the month` (YMD 2025 12 15) `with suspension` (JUST `a suspension from 15 September 2025 until payment resumed in December 2025`))
-- Taking effect on the first of a month: that month is suspended throughout.
#ASSERT `the person is eligible to receive an allocation for the month` (`an otherwise eligible person in the month` (YMD 2025 9 15) `with suspension` (JUST `a suspension from 1 October 2025 until payment resumed in December 2025`))
#ASSERT NOT `the person is eligible to receive an allocation for the month` (`an otherwise eligible person in the month` (YMD 2025 10 15) `with suspension` (JUST `a suspension from 1 October 2025 until payment resumed in December 2025`))
-- Taking effect on the last day of August (the default in s 11(2)(a)): August is paid,
-- September onward is not, for as long as payment never resumes.
#ASSERT `the person is eligible to receive an allocation for the month` (`an otherwise eligible person in the month` (YMD 2025 7 15) `with suspension` (JUST `a suspension from 31 August 2025 with no resumption`))
#ASSERT `the person is eligible to receive an allocation for the month` (`an otherwise eligible person in the month` (YMD 2025 8 15) `with suspension` (JUST `a suspension from 31 August 2025 with no resumption`))
#ASSERT NOT `the person is eligible to receive an allocation for the month` (`an otherwise eligible person in the month` (YMD 2025 9 15) `with suspension` (JUST `a suspension from 31 August 2025 with no resumption`))
#ASSERT NOT `the person is eligible to receive an allocation for the month` (`an otherwise eligible person in the month` (YMD 2026 8 15) `with suspension` (JUST `a suspension from 31 August 2025 with no resumption`))

§ `Regulations s 2.1 and the related provision SOR/2026-123 s 14 -- tests`

`an allocation payment the person was entitled to, on a status that rests on the certificate` MEANS `Payment made after a certificate` WITH
    `the payment is an allocation` IS TRUE
    `the payment was made before SOR/2026-123 section 14 came into force` IS FALSE
    `the person was entitled to the payment` IS TRUE
    `the status as a DTC-eligible individual at the time of the payment rests on that certificate` IS TRUE

`an earlier benefit payment deemed to be an allocation` MEANS `Payment made after a certificate` WITH
    `the payment is an allocation` IS FALSE
    `the payment was made before SOR/2026-123 section 14 came into force` IS TRUE
    `the person was entitled to the payment` IS TRUE
    `the status as a DTC-eligible individual at the time of the payment rests on that certificate` IS TRUE

`a payment the person was not entitled to` MEANS `Payment made after a certificate` WITH
    `the payment is an allocation` IS TRUE
    `the payment was made before SOR/2026-123 section 14 came into force` IS FALSE
    `the person was entitled to the payment` IS FALSE
    `the status as a DTC-eligible individual at the time of the payment rests on that certificate` IS TRUE

`a payment on a status resting on another certificate` MEANS `Payment made after a certificate` WITH
    `the payment is an allocation` IS TRUE
    `the payment was made before SOR/2026-123 section 14 came into force` IS FALSE
    `the person was entitled to the payment` IS TRUE
    `the status as a DTC-eligible individual at the time of the payment rests on that certificate` IS FALSE

`a payment that is neither an allocation nor an earlier benefit payment` MEANS `Payment made after a certificate` WITH
    `the payment is an allocation` IS FALSE
    `the payment was made before SOR/2026-123 section 14 came into force` IS FALSE
    `the person was entitled to the payment` IS TRUE
    `the status as a DTC-eligible individual at the time of the payment rests on that certificate` IS TRUE

#ASSERT `a supplemental amount is owed for the certificate` TRUE (LIST `an allocation payment the person was entitled to, on a status that rests on the certificate`)
-- Related provision: an earlier benefit payment is deemed to be an allocation.
#ASSERT `a supplemental amount is owed for the certificate` TRUE (LIST `an earlier benefit payment deemed to be an allocation`)
-- 2.1(2): a payment the person was not entitled to is not considered.
#ASSERT NOT `a supplemental amount is owed for the certificate` TRUE (LIST `a payment the person was not entitled to`)
#ASSERT NOT `a supplemental amount is owed for the certificate` TRUE (LIST `a payment on a status resting on another certificate`)
#ASSERT NOT `a supplemental amount is owed for the certificate` TRUE (LIST `a payment that is neither an allocation nor an earlier benefit payment`)
-- No certificate, or no payment after it: nothing is owed.
#ASSERT NOT `a supplemental amount is owed for the certificate` FALSE (LIST `an allocation payment the person was entitled to, on a status that rests on the certificate`)
#ASSERT NOT `a supplemental amount is owed for the certificate` TRUE (EMPTY)
-- One qualifying payment among several is enough.
#ASSERT `a supplemental amount is owed for the certificate` TRUE (LIST `a payment the person was not entitled to`, `an allocation payment the person was entitled to, on a status that rests on the certificate`)

§§ `s 2(4) and s 2(6) override the exceptions in s 2(2) and s 2(3) (finding 10)`

-- A person with a cohabiting spouse or partner who has not filed, varying the birth date, the
-- month and the custody; the Minister has not waived the condition.
GIVEN filed   IS A BOOLEAN
      dob     IS A DATE
      month   IS A DATE
      custody IS A MAYBE `Custody under a sentence`
GIVETH A `Person facts for a month`
`a person with a spouse who has filed` filed `born on` dob `asking about` month `with custody` custody MEANS
    `Person facts for a month` WITH
        `the month asked about`                       IS month
        `date of birth`                               IS dob
        `a DTC-eligible individual throughout the month` IS TRUE
        `resident in Canada for the purposes of the Income Tax Act throughout the month` IS TRUE
        `a Canadian citizen`                          IS TRUE
        `a permanent resident`                        IS FALSE
        `a temporary resident`                        IS FALSE
        `months resident in Canada immediately before the month` IS 0
        `a protected person`                          IS FALSE
        `an Indian as defined in subsection 2(1) of the Indian Act` IS FALSE
        `the custody under a sentence`                IS custody
        `a return of income was filed for the last taxation year that ended before the payment period began` IS TRUE
        `a cohabiting spouse or common-law partner on the last day of the month before` IS TRUE
        `the cohabiting spouse or common-law partner filed a return of income for that year` IS filed
        `the Minister waived the spouse or partner condition` IS FALSE
        `the suspension the beneficiary asked for`    IS NOTHING

-- The month of the 65th birthday (s 2(2)): eligible when the partner filed, not when they did not.
#ASSERT `the person is eligible to receive an allocation for the month` (`a person with a spouse who has filed` TRUE `born on` (YMD 1960 8 20) `asking about` (YMD 2025 8 15) `with custody` NOTHING)
#ASSERT NOT `the person is eligible to receive an allocation for the month` (`a person with a spouse who has filed` FALSE `born on` (YMD 1960 8 20) `asking about` (YMD 2025 8 15) `with custody` NOTHING)
-- The month of the release (s 2(3)): the same.
#ASSERT `the person is eligible to receive an allocation for the month` (`a person with a spouse who has filed` TRUE `born on` (YMD 1990 5 10) `asking about` (YMD 2025 9 15) `with custody` (JUST `the same custody ended by expiry on 10 September 2025`))
#ASSERT NOT `the person is eligible to receive an allocation for the month` (`a person with a spouse who has filed` FALSE `born on` (YMD 1990 5 10) `asking about` (YMD 2025 9 15) `with custody` (JUST `the same custody ended by expiry on 10 September 2025`))
-- The first month of the incarceration (s 2(3)): the same.
#ASSERT `the person is eligible to receive an allocation for the month` (`a person with a spouse who has filed` TRUE `born on` (YMD 1990 5 10) `asking about` (YMD 2025 6 15) `with custody` (JUST `a qualifying custody from 20 June 2025`))
#ASSERT NOT `the person is eligible to receive an allocation for the month` (`a person with a spouse who has filed` FALSE `born on` (YMD 1990 5 10) `asking about` (YMD 2025 6 15) `with custody` (JUST `a qualifying custody from 20 June 2025`))

-- s 2(6) also begins "Despite subsections (1) to (3)": a person in the month of the 65th birthday
-- whose payment is suspended throughout that month (a suspension in force since 1 October 2025
-- here) is ineligible, and is eligible in the month before the suspension.
GIVEN dob   IS A DATE
      month IS A DATE
      susp  IS A MAYBE `Suspension at the beneficiary's request`
GIVETH A `Person facts for a month`
`a person born on` dob `asking about` month `with the suspension` susp MEANS
    `Person facts for a month` WITH
        `the month asked about`                       IS month
        `date of birth`                               IS dob
        `a DTC-eligible individual throughout the month` IS TRUE
        `resident in Canada for the purposes of the Income Tax Act throughout the month` IS TRUE
        `a Canadian citizen`                          IS TRUE
        `a permanent resident`                        IS FALSE
        `a temporary resident`                        IS FALSE
        `months resident in Canada immediately before the month` IS 0
        `a protected person`                          IS FALSE
        `an Indian as defined in subsection 2(1) of the Indian Act` IS FALSE
        `the custody under a sentence`                IS NOTHING
        `a return of income was filed for the last taxation year that ended before the payment period began` IS TRUE
        `a cohabiting spouse or common-law partner on the last day of the month before` IS FALSE
        `the cohabiting spouse or common-law partner filed a return of income for that year` IS FALSE
        `the Minister waived the spouse or partner condition` IS FALSE
        `the suspension the beneficiary asked for`    IS susp

#ASSERT NOT `the person is eligible to receive an allocation for the month` (`a person born on` (YMD 1960 10 20) `asking about` (YMD 2025 10 15) `with the suspension` (JUST `a suspension from 1 October 2025 until payment resumed in December 2025`))
#ASSERT `the person is eligible to receive an allocation for the month` (`a person born on` (YMD 1960 9 20) `asking about` (YMD 2025 9 15) `with the suspension` (JUST `a suspension from 1 October 2025 until payment resumed in December 2025`))
